lt-in speakers is  really kind of a nightmare  dell also sells a 2099 dollar model  which has the same Nvidia 1650 graphics  card but with a 6 core processor which  is a much better pairing and in many  cases like video editing gaming and  other GPU intensive uses the actual  performance will be exactly the same  that spec still comes with a one  terabyte SSD but only with 16 gigabytes  of RAM but you can easily change that  and very affordably upgrade it to 32  gigabytes you won't get OLED but it's  still a 4k display that is very colored  accurate so even though I wouldn't  recommend the 8 core OLED XPS 15 for  serious video editors if you're somebody  that doesn't need the latest and  greatest bleeding-edge in terms of  performance the 6 core non OLED model is  a great bang for the buck  overall the Dell XPS 15 isn't perfect  and we wish that they would have made  more external changes like adding more  Thunderbolt 3 ports windows hello and  better speakers it's still a fantastic  all-around value especially for those  that really need to have a good  BPU and not to forget this laptop is  still fairly upgradable down the line  where much of the competition isn't  thank you guys for watching this has  been max with Max tech if you guys want  to see more videos like this one click  that little circle above and then down  below hit the notification bell if you  want to be notified when we post new  videos and if you guys want to see a  comparison between the Dell XPS and the  MacBook Pro you guys can click them  right over there I will see you guys in  the next video  [Music]

